Two independent iOS fixes for pyproj's extension link: let the recipe name
the libraries to link, and stop asking for a runtime library search path on
a platform that has neither a shared libproj nor a linker that accepts the
flag.

pyproj is already environment-driven where paths are concerned —
`get_proj_dir()`/`get_proj_libdirs()`/`get_proj_incdirs()` honour `PROJ_DIR`,
`PROJ_LIBDIR` and `PROJ_INCDIR`, and `PROJ_VERSION` short-circuits the
version probe that would otherwise execute `$PROJ_DIR/bin/proj` (a target
binary the macOS build host cannot run, and one `flet-libproj`'s build.sh
deletes anyway with `rm -rf $PREFIX/{bin,share}`). This recipe therefore
only needs `PROJ_DIR: {platlib}/opt` and `PROJ_VERSION: 9.5.0` in
`script_env`, and the two gaps below.

  1. `get_libraries()` hard-wires `libraries = ["proj"]` (the only override
     is a Windows `.lib` glob). On Android that is right: libproj is a
     shared object and the loader pulls its dependencies in behind it, so
     `meta.yaml` sets no `PROJ_LIBS` and the default stands. On iOS
     `flet-libproj` is built `-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF`, and when `libproj.a`
     was archived the linker kept only the objects proj itself referenced —
     its calls into libtiff (grid files), libcurl + libpsl (the network grid
     fetcher), libsqlite3 (proj.db) and openssl (HTTPS under libcurl) were
     left undefined. `_geod`/`_crs`/`_context` inherit those undefined
     references, `-undefined dynamic_lookup` defers them to dlopen, and iOS
     dyld resolves the flat namespace eagerly and aborts on the first miss —
     observed landing on `_TIFFClientOpen`. The hunk lets
     `PROJ_LIBS=proj,tiff,curl,psl,sqlite3,jpeg,ssl,crypto,z` (comma-
     separated; library names, not paths) replace the list so pyproj's own
     link pulls those objects straight out of the archives. `meta.yaml`
     carries the fuller version and points at the real fix, which belongs in
     `flet-libproj`'s iOS cmake call.

  2. `ext_options["runtime_library_dirs"]` is set to `library_dirs` on
     everything except Windows and cygwin. That asks distutils for a runtime
     search path, and
     `setuptools._distutils.unixccompiler.runtime_library_dir_option()`
     picks its spelling from `sys.platform`. Inside forge's crossenv that is
     the *target* platform, not the host: crossenv takes it from the first
     field of the host platform identifier
     (`crossenv/__init__.py`, `host_sys_platform`), and forge builds that
     identifier as `ios-<version>-<arch>-<sdk>`
     (`src/forge/cross.py::_platform_identifier`) — so `sys.platform` is
     `"ios"`, the `darwin` branch is skipped, and the option falls through to
     the GNU-linker fallbacks at the bottom of that function: `-Wl,-R<dir>`,
     or `-Wl,--enable-new-dtags` plus `-Wl,-rpath,<dir>` if the sysconfig
     claims GNU ld. Apple's ld64 takes neither spelling. Adding `ios` to the
     exclusion makes `runtime_library_dirs` `None` on those slices.

     The change is right on its own terms, too: on iOS libproj is a static
     archive absorbed into each extension, so there is no shared library to
     find at load time and a runtime search path is meaningless — at best it
     would bake a build-machine directory into the shipped binary. Android
     is deliberately left alone: `sys.platform` there is `"android"`, so it
     takes the same fallback branch, but the NDK's lld does accept `-R` (its
     GNU alias for `-rpath`), and the resulting build-host RUNPATH is simply
     ignored by the Android loader, which resolves from the APK's `lib/`.

Hunk 1's rationale is recorded: it arrived with PR #65 ("Support testing
recipes on Android emulator and iOS simulator and fixes issues found"),
which documents this dyld flat-namespace cascade across the GDAL/PROJ
recipes. Hunk 2 predates it, arriving in the bulk consolidation commit
ec8d184, which records no per-patch reason and no linker diagnostic; the
mechanism described above is read off distutils' source and forge's own
crossenv setup rather than from a captured build log, so the exact error
text that motivated it is not known.

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -155,6 +155,8 @@
     This function gets the libraries to cythonize with
     """
     libraries = ["proj"]
+    if "PROJ_LIBS" in os.environ:
+        libraries = os.environ["PROJ_LIBS"].split(",")
     if os.name == "nt":
         for libdir in libdirs:
             projlib = list(Path(libdir).glob("proj*.lib"))
@@ -194,7 +196,9 @@ def get_extension_modules():
         "include_dirs": include_dirs,
         "library_dirs": library_dirs,
         "runtime_library_dirs": (
-            library_dirs if os.name != "nt" and sys.platform != "cygwin" else None
+            library_dirs
+            if os.name != "nt" and sys.platform != "cygwin" and sys.platform != "ios"
+            else None
         ),
         "libraries": get_libraries(library_dirs),
     }
